<div style="background-color: #d0e4f7; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.2em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> An Environmental Project</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Let's Recycle Our Paper!</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: text: Write simple interpretations of common texts in English supported with visual aids. communication: Facilitate a discussion on a group project.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can write a simple interpretation of common texts with visual aids (e.g., write 'recycle paper' and show a recycling symbol). Can facilitate a group project discussion by writing prompts and showing visuals (e.g., 'Who wants to write the title of the project on the board?' and holds up a marker, helping the team decide who will take that role.). Can use visual aids and simple phrases to clarify project instructions for peers (e.g., holds up a drawing of sorting bins and says, 'This is the blue bin for paper.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #e6f2ff;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows a picture of a trash bin overflowing with paper and then a picture of a recycling bin with paper. The teacher asks, "What do you see?" and "Which picture is good for our environment?" Students share their ideas using simple phrases. The teacher holds up a "Recycle Paper" sign and asks students to repeat "Recycle paper!" focusing on clear pronunciation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up a picture of a blue recycling bin and says, "This is the blue bin for paper. We will put paper here." The teacher then holds up a marker and a blank poster board, saying, "I will write 'Recycle Paper' here." The teacher models pronouncing 'will' /wɪl/ clearly and slowly, and then the contracted form 'I'll' /aɪl/ when showing how they'll help prepare the project materials.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is this for plastic or paper?" (pointing to a blue bin picture).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Will we throw paper in the trash?" (shakes head 'no').</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents a "Classroom Recycling Campaign" poster (genre: informational poster) with simple text and clear visuals. The poster includes:
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A large recycling symbol and the words "Recycle Paper!"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">An image of a blue bin with "Put paper here."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">An image of a tree and the text "We will help plants and trees!"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A calendar image with "Presentation Day: Next Friday!"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will learn to interpret simple written texts and visual aids related to an environmental project.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher points to parts of the poster and asks "What does this symbol mean?" or "What do we put in the blue bin?" (Gist questions).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">True/False statements: "We will save trees by recycling. True or False?" or "The presentation day is tomorrow. True or False?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice mediating information using future simple ('We will plant trees'), imperatives ('Put paper here'), present simple ('We usually sort'), and target vocabulary (project, environment, clean, plant, recycle, presentation day). Focus on pronunciation of 'will' /wɪl/ and segmenting 'presentation' into 'pre-sen-ta-tion'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled practice:</b> Students receive a worksheet with pictures of recycling actions (e.g., sorting paper, a blue bin) and a list of simple sentences. They match the picture to the correct sentence. Examples: "Put paper in the blue bin." "We will clean the classroom." "This project will help the environment."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled practice (Substitution Drill):</b> Teacher writes sentence frames on the board, like "We will _______ paper." Students complete with verbs like 'recycle', 'collect', 'save'. Or, "_______ paper in the bin!" Students use imperatives like 'Put', 'Place', 'Bring'. Students practice pronouncing 'will' and 'I'll' correctly as they say their sentences.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction / Peer Check:</b> In pairs, students receive flashcards with simple recycling instructions (e.g., "Bring your old notebooks," "Separate paper from plastic") and other flashcards with corresponding visuals. Student A reads an instruction, and Student B finds the correct visual. Then they switch roles. They check each other's matches and help clarify using simple phrases like "No, this is for paper."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">12-15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students) to develop a part of their "Classroom Recycling Campaign." Each group focuses on mediating a specific aspect of the project.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Discussion and Mini-Presentation/Explanation.
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group is given a specific task related to the campaign:
                            <ol style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Group 1: Explain "Why recycle paper?" using a visual and simple sentences like, "We will help the environment."</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Group 2: Show "How to recycle paper in our classroom" using drawings of bins and imperatives like, "Put paper in the blue bin!"</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Group 3: Announce the "Presentation Day" and what to bring, using phrases like, "Bring old paper!" and showing a calendar visual.</li>
                            </ol>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students use visual aids (pictures, simple drawings, flashcards) to explain their part of the campaign to their peers. One student acts as a facilitator, writing simple prompts on a small board or showing cards to help the group decide roles or clarify ideas (e.g., holding up a marker and saying, "Who wants to write 'Recycle Paper' for our project?").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They use grammar points (future simple, imperatives, present simple) and vocabulary from the theme. They practice segmenting words like 'presentation' if they use the word.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in explaining, collaborative interaction, and successful completion of their campaign segment using visual mediation.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on students' ability to mediate information effectively using visuals and clear language.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their campaign segment to the class. Students are assessed on their individual contribution to mediating the information within their group's presentation/explanation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity:</b> Can they clearly explain their part of the project using simple English?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Visual Aids:</b> Do they effectively use visual aids to support their explanation (e.g., showing a recycling symbol, picture of a blue bin)?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Language Use:</b> Do they use target vocabulary (e.g., project, environment, recycle, plants) and grammar (imperatives, future simple) correctly?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Is their pronunciation of 'will' and multi-syllabic words like 'presentation' intelligible?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Do they work well as a team, facilitating discussion or clarifying for peers?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick exit ticket:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can explain 'Why recycle paper!' using a picture." (Yes/No/A little)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can use a picture to show 'Put paper in the blue bin!'" (Yes/No/A little)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy to explain using pictures today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What can I do better next time to help my friends understand our project?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What worked well in mediating the recycling campaign? The use of visual aids was effective, and students actively participated in the group discussions. Some students struggled with consistently using the future simple tense for plans; more focused practice will be needed in future lessons. Providing sentence starters for facilitating discussions would also be helpful. The segmenting of 'presentation' was a good phonemic awareness activity.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson concludes the "Let's Recycle Our Paper!" theme. The next lesson will introduce a new theme and set of vocabulary, potentially focusing on another environmental aspect or community project, building on the collaboration and presentation skills developed here.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>